\ Constructing and reading non-builtin values under `--interpreter-fallback=false
\ --lock-interpreter-setting`. The lock rejects every fallback emission, so a
\ construction native that compiles to `jitNativeWordCall` makes the whole
\ category of virtual-type and struct values unbuildable.
\
\ The three construction natives are reached only through their `native.`-qualified
\ names, and the AOT direct-wrapper table is keyed by the name codegen resolves, so
\ each one compiles to a direct call.
\
\ Observation is constrained by the lock itself. `.` needs a proven parameter type
\ before `inspect` monomorphizes, so each value is compared against a literal and a
\ fixed string is printed.

boxed:   virtual{ fixnum } ;
point:   struct{ x y } ;
inner:   struct{ a } ;
wrapped: virtual{ inner } ;

\ native.virtual-wrap
5 make-boxed unmake-boxed 5 = [ "virtual ok" ] [ "virtual wrong" ] if print-line

\ native.make-struct-instance, then native.struct-field-get through the getter
3 4 make-point x>> 3 = [ "struct ok" ] [ "struct wrong" ] if print-line
3 4 make-point y>> 4 = [ "struct getter ok" ] [ "struct getter wrong" ] if print-line

\ native.virtual-struct-wrap and native.virtual-struct-unwrap
7 make-inner make-wrapped unmake-wrapped a>> 7 = [ "virtual struct ok" ] [ "virtual struct wrong" ] if print-line
